{"name":"Fossilised","hex":"#b6b8b0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fossilised","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Non-Oxford British English standard spelling of fossilized."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fossilised"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fossil","blocks":[{"text":"A fossil is any preserved remains, impression, or trace of any once-living thing from a past geological age. Examples include bones, shells, exoskeletons, stone imprints of animals or microbes, objects preserved in amber, hair, petrified wood and DNA remnants. The totality of fossils is known as the fossil record. Though the fossil record is incomplete, numerous studies have demonstrated that there is enough information available to give a good understanding of the pattern of diversification of life on Earth, and it can fill gaps in our understanding of the sequence of evolution on earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Fossil_Diversity.png/330px-Fossil_Diversity.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fossil"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tyrannosaurus_Rex_Holotype.jpg/500px-Tyrannosaurus_Rex_Holotype.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tyrannosaurus_Rex_Holotype.jpg/1280px-Tyrannosaurus_Rex_Holotype.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tyrannosaurus_Rex_Holotype.jpg/500px-Tyrannosaurus_Rex_Holotype.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATyrannosaurus_Rex_Holotype.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Hyperborean-gryphon-persepolis-protoceratops-psittacosaurus-skeletons.jpg/500px-Hyperborean-gryphon-persepolis-protoceratops-psittacosaurus-skeletons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Hyperborean-gryphon-persepolis-protoceratops-psittacosaurus-skeletons.jpg/1280px-Hyperborean-gryphon-persepolis-protoceratops-psittacosaurus-skeletons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Hyperborean-gryphon-persepolis-protoceratops-psittacosaurus-skeletons.jpg/500px-Hyperborean-gryphon-persepolis-protoceratops-psittacosaurus-skeletons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ceratopsian skulls are common in the Dzungarian Gate mountain pass in Asia, an area once famous for gold mines and cold winds. This has been attributed to legends of both gryphons and the land of Hyperborea.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHyperborean-gryphon-persepolis-protoceratops-psittacosaurus-skeletons.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Micraster_coranguinum.4_-_Cretacico_superior.JPG/500px-Micraster_coranguinum.4_-_Cretacico_superior.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Micraster_coranguinum.4_-_Cretacico_superior.JPG/1280px-Micraster_coranguinum.4_-_Cretacico_superior.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Micraster_coranguinum.4_-_Cretacico_superior.JPG/500px-Micraster_coranguinum.4_-_Cretacico_superior.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fossil shells from the cretaceous era sea urchin, Micraster, were used in medieval times as both shepherd's crowns to protect houses, and as painted fairy loaves by bakers to bring luck to their b